  "fields": {
    "title": "Content Management System",
    "textContent": {
      "nodeType": "document",
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Description",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "A content management system (CMS) is a software for collaborative creation, editing, organisation and presentation of digital content, mostly websites. This content can consist of text and multimedia documents. An author with appropriate access rights can operate such a system in many cases with little or no knowledge of programming or HTML, as the majority of systems have a ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "1DDBuJHPyDiiT0BOAEo8V6",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "graphical user interface",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": ". Some also offer a ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "7gVQobWbxFti05whwYInu5",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "no-code editor",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " or templates. The most popular CMS is probably Wordpress, but there are a lot more, we use for example Contentful on this website. But you could also use other software, like Google Sheets or Notion as a CMS.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "The implementation of a CMS is quite useful when developing a website for clients, so they can adapt the content of the page themselves. It is also useful to ensure the easy management of content, especially for large websites such as online magazines with many articles. Most CMS offer a templating engine and an API, that you can integrate in your code. ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
